{"result":0,"text":"Tom set down his pot and rose from the bench, the wood creaking as he stood. He crossed the taproom toward the bar, six paces over the flagstones, past the tables where the talk of travellers murmured on. The drizzle still ticked at the dark windows, and the fire burned low behind him."},
{"result":2,"text":"He reached the bar in a few seconds, boots quiet on the boards, and leaned in so the boy behind it could hear him without the room hearing."},
{"result":3,"text":"Tom spoke in a low, steady voice, close to the innkeeper's ear: two men at the table by the fire were plotting to take a chest from a wagon at the ford below the bridge before dawn, when the moon set. The boy heard every word plainly, his cloth going still in his hand, and his eyes flicked past Tom's shoulder toward the fire."},
{"result":4,"text":"Across the room, the two men at the next table had marked him. At six paces, by the light of the taproom, they could see plainly that Tom had left his seat and was speaking quietly with the innkeeper, and their whispering stopped."},
